{"code": 200, "data": {"additional_feedback": "", "aiWords": 36, "fakePercentage": 23.7, "feedback": "Your Text is Most Likely Human written, may include parts generated by AI/GPT", "h": ["This could mix timer/background threads with Swing/JavaFX and lead to threading issues (e.g. the application not exiting cleanly).", "Fix: Ensure the call to open the JavaFX dialog is first posted to the Swing event dispatch thread."], "hi": [], "id": 59224931, "input_text": "Problem: A TimerTask called DefaultTaskExecutor.runInJavaFXThread directly from the timer thread to show the tracking/statistics notification. This could mix timer/background threads with Swing/JavaFX and lead to threading issues (e.g. the application not exiting cleanly).

Fix: Ensure the call to open the JavaFX dialog is first posted to the Swing event dispatch thread. The TimerTask now wraps the call in SwingUtilities.invokeLater(...) which then calls DefaultTaskExecutor.runInJavaFXThread(JabRefFrame::showTrackingNotification). This guarantees the UI work is forwarded from the EDT into JavaFX correctly.

Impact: Thread-safety and lifecycle issues when showing the tracking/statistics notification are addressed. No functional UI changes, only safer threading behavior.", "isHuman": 75.0, "originalParagraph": "2026/8/30/ac0565a7-f2bb-499c-b3c2-4218bc74bf17", "sentences": [], "specialIndexes": [], "specialSentences": [], "textWords": 96}, "message": "Detection complete", "success": true}

